[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/slash_arc.gd" id="1_script"]

; ── Magical energy-sword cut — iter 75 swept-blade rework ────────────────
; The previous (iter 73) build layered HiltFlash + GhostArc + 3 arc
; Line2Ds + 2 particle bursts, but user feedback said it still read as a
; "weird drawn-on thing in front of the character" rather than a swung
; energy blade. Diagnosis: an arc shape is geometric, not motion. The
; eye does not parse "static curved decoration" as a swung weapon.
;
; Iter 75 reframes the slash around a SWEPT BLADE — a thin glowing line
; that ACTUALLY rotates from start_angle → end_angle, leaving the arc
; trail behind it as residual energy. The eye traces the tip's path
; through space; the arc becomes the wake, not the swing itself.
;
; Read order (Phase 1 → Phase 5):
;   Phase 1: BladeRig — a Node2D that rotates. Its local rotation sweeps
;            from -SWING_HALF*sign to +SWING_HALF*sign across SWING_TIME.
;            Children rotate with it. Pivot is at origin (hero's hand).
;   Phase 2: BladeGlow / Blade — two-point Line2Ds along +X from origin
;            to tip, tapered widths. BladeGlow sits behind for the halo
;            spread; Blade is the bright cyan-white core edge.
;   Phase 3: GhostArc / OuterHalo / Halo / Core — the existing iter-73
;            arc layers, repurposed as the residual wake. Their alpha
;            ramps IN with TRAIL_DELAY (so the blade visibly leads) and
;            fades on the longer DURATION tail.
;   Phase 4: TipBurst is parented to BladeRig so its spark stream tracks
;            the rotating tip — sparks fly off WHERE THE BLADE IS, not
;            where it WAS.
;   Phase 5: HiltFlash (anticipation) + HiltSparkle (channeling) stay
;            anchored to the origin (Node2D root) — they don't rotate.
;
; Layer order (back → front in tree):
;   GhostArc        — widest, lowest-alpha trail (was iter-73 motion blur)
;   OuterHalo       — wide purple-magenta wake
;   Halo            — mid gold-magenta wake
;   Core            — narrow cream-white wake edge
;   BladeRig (rotates)
;     ├─ BladeGlow  — wider tapered glow line, 9 → 3
;     ├─ Blade      — bright cyan-white core line, 4 → 1
;     └─ TipBurst   — sparks at the rotating tip
;   HiltSparkle     — magenta channeling at origin (no rotation)
;   HiltFlash       — bright cyan-white anticipation pulse (no rotation)

